# Domain vs persistence

Follow `backend/AGENTS.md`. When adding data:

1. Domain type in `backend/src/domain/` — `id: string`, no mongoose, no password.
2. Schema in `backend/src/models/` — `InferSchemaType` + `HydratedDocument`, not `extends Document`.
3. Repository in `backend/src/repositories/` — maps `_id` → `id`; only file that imports `*Model`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — route/service talks to mongoose
const doc = await UserModel.findOne({ email });
res.json(doc);

// ✅ GOOD
const user = await findUserByEmail(email);
if (!user) throw new NotFoundException("User not found");
res.json(user);
```

Do not add a generic `Repository<T>`. Do not use `schema.pre("save")` to hash passwords. Hash in `services/user.service.ts` (`registerUser`, `setUserPassword`), then store via `createUser({ passwordHash })`. Login may use `findUserCredentialsByEmail` + `comparePassword`.
